<h1>Email Keeper — Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="muted">Last updated: October 26, 2026</p>

<h2>Who we are</h2>
<p>Email Keeper (Android app <code>com.usefulappz.emailkeeper</code>) is developed by Usefulappz™ (Mike Kelley). Contact: <a href="mailto:mikekelleyii.mk2@gmail.com">mikekelleyii.mk2@gmail.com</a></p>

<h2>The short version</h2>
<p>Email Keeper is a status board for the developer's own mailboxes. It shows whether each mailbox can still be read — up or down, and when it was last checked. It collects <strong>no data from you</strong>: no accounts, no analytics, no ads SDK, no tracking, and nothing is sold.</p>

<h2>How the app works</h2>
<ul>
  <li>The status itself is computed on <strong>our server</strong>, which performs scheduled read-only checks against the developer's own six mailboxes. The checks test whether a mailbox can be read; they never sign in, never send mail, and never read or store message content.</li>
  <li>The app fetches that board — mailbox names, up/down status, and the time of the last check — from our server and displays it. That is the app's only network call, and it carries none of your information.</li>
</ul>

<h2>What the app stores</h2>
<p>Nothing about you. The app keeps no account, no profile, and no usage data. The board it displays describes the developer's mailboxes, not your device.</p>

<h2>Permissions, and why</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Internet</strong> — used only to fetch the mailbox status board from our server, as described above.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Ads</h2>
<p>Email Keeper contains <strong>no ads and no advertising SDK</strong>.</p>

<h2>Children</h2>
<p>Email Keeper is a tool for the developer's own operations. It is not directed at children under 13, and it collects no data from anyone.</p>

<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>If this policy changes, the new version will be posted at this URL with a new "last updated" date.</p>

